{"author":{"id":"417295a7cc0952a9a38b67be3a894daed91f9069f7407e038d12a4f9b9a8451e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792345157,"nonce":"6BVHrQdLe5Qv2sRpYZGEd8QL4mY=","message":"Diagnostics now render with ariadne 0.6 (byte offsets). Diagnostic::render is plain ASCII for logs and thrown strings; render_with(.., true) and Vm::set_fancy_errors add colour and Unicode, which the CLI turns on when stderr is a terminal and NO_COLOR is unset. Diagnostics carry a caption and secondary labels (unclosed ( [ { and mismatched tags point at the opener). Failed fibers are reported as one ariadne report across modules: the raising line, then the nearest 8 calls, then a count. Wrapping note: an import that fails to compile throws its rendered report, so the importer's failure reads 'Error: Error: ...'; a structured cause on Failure would fix it.","files":null}]}